hadiths[27]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27295","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, that Umar ibn al-Khattab found the scent of perfume at Dhu al-Hulayfah and said: From whom is this scent. Muawiyah said: From me, O Commander of the Believers. He said: From you, by my life. He said: Umm Habibah perfumed me, and claimed she perfumed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at his ihram. He said: Go and adjure her to wash it. So he returned to her and she washed it."
"27296","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Suwayd ibn Qays, from Muawiyah ibn Hudayj, from Muawiyah, he said: I said to Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: Did the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, pray in the garment he sleeps with you in. She said: Yes, as long as he saw no harm in it."
"27297","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Damrah ibn Habib narrated to us, that Muhammad ibn Abi Sufyan al-Thaqafi narrated to him, that he heard Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying, with upon me and upon him one garment, in which was what was."
"27298","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abi al-Duha, from Shutayr ibn Shakl, from Umm Habibah, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to kiss while fasting."
"27299","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from Abi al-Jarrah, the freed slave of Umm Habibah, from Umm Habibah, that she narrated to him, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: Were it not to burden my ummah, I would command them with siwak at every prayer as they perform ablution."
"27300","Rawh narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyyah, he said: When death came to Anbasah ibn Abi Sufyan, his panic intensified. It was said to him: What is this panic. He said: I heard Umm Habibah, meaning his sister, saying: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever prays four before Zuhr and four after it, Allah will forbid his flesh upon the Fire. I have not left them since I heard them."
"27301","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Bakr, from Humayd ibn Nafi, that Zaynab bint Abi Salama informed him that she entered upon Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan, and she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three nights, except over a husband, four months and ten days. My father said: Humayd ibn Nafi is Abu Aflah, and he is Humayd Sughayra."
"27302","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, and Hajjaj said: Shuba narrated to me, from Humayd ibn Nafi, he said: I heard Zaynab bint Umm Salama say: A relative of Umm Habiba died, so she called for yellow perfume and wiped her forearms with it, and said: I only do this because of something I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, and Hajjaj said: Because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn for more than three, except over her husband, four months and ten days. And Zaynab narrated to him from her mother, and from Zaynab the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or from a woman among some of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"27303","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Abu al-Malih, from Umm Habiba, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he heard the muadhdhin calling the adhan, he would say as he says until he falls silent."
"27304","Bahz narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Bahdala narrated to us, from Abu Salih, that Umm Habiba narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Whoever prays in a day twelve rakas, Allah will build for him, or there will be built for him, a house in Paradise."
"27305","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from al-Musayyab ibn Rafi, from Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever prays in a day and night twelve prostrations apart from the obligatory prayer, a house will be built for him in Paradise."
"27306","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shuayb narrated to us, he said: Nafi said: Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar informed me that Abu al-Jarrah, the freed slave of Umm Habiba the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to Abd Allah ibn Umar that Umm Habiba informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the caravan in which there is a bell will not be accompanied by the angels."
"27307","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: I heard him narrating, meaning his father, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn Usama ibn al-Had, that Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar narrated to him that Abu al-Jarrah, the freed slave of Umm Habiba, informed him that Umm Habiba the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels do not accompany a people among whom there is a bell."
"27308","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahia narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to us, Makhul informed me that a freed slave of Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to him that Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan informed him, from Umm Habiba bint Abi Sufyan, that she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever prays four before Zhuhr and four after Zhuhr, Allah will forbid him to the Fire."
"27309","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Aban, meaning Ibn Yazid al-Attar, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama, from Abu Sufyan ibn Said ibn al-Mughira, that he entered upon Umm Habiba the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she gave him a cup of sawiq to drink, so he called for water and rinsed his mouth, and she said to him: O son of my brother, will you not perform ablution, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched, or has altered."
"27310","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal, meaning Ibn Fudala, narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Ata, that he said: Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to us, he said: I heard Umm Habiba, the Mother of the Believers, say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever prays twelve rakas in his night and day apart from the obligatory prayer, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise."
"27311","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Salim, from Amr ibn Aws, from Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan, from his sister Umm Habiba the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no Muslim servant who prays to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, every day twelve rakas as voluntary prayer apart from the obligatory prayer, except that a house will be built for him in Paradise, or Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will build for him by them a house in Paradise. So Umm Habiba said: I have not ceased praying them since. And Amr said: I have not ceased praying them since. And al-Numan said the like of that."
"27312","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ata informed me, from Ibn Shawwal, that he informed him that he entered upon Umm Habiba, and she informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent her ahead from Muzdalifa by night."
"27313","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, he said: Nafi informed me, from Salim, from Abu al-Jarrah, from Umm Habiba, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell."
"27314","Waki narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salama narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Sufyan ibn Akhnas, from Umm Habiba the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she was his maternal aunt, he said: She gave me sawiq to drink, then she said: Do not go out until you perform ablution, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"27315","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Abu Sufyan ibn Said, from Umm Habiba, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"27316","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi, from Salim ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Jarrah the freed slave of Umm Habiba, from Umm Habiba, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed the caravan in which there is a bell will not be accompanied by the angels."
"27317","Bahz and Ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Shuba narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Salim, he said: I heard Amr ibn Aws narrating from Anbasa, from Umm Habiba, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no Muslim servant who performs ablution and perfects the ablution, then prays to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, every day twelve rakas, except that a house will be built for him in Paradise. Umm Habiba said: I have not ceased praying them since. And Anbasa said: I have not ceased praying them since. And Amr ibn Aws said: I have not ceased praying them. Al-Numan said: And I hardly ever leave them. Ibn Jafar said: From Anbasa ibn Abi Sufyan, from Umm Habiba the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no Muslim servant who prays to Allah, Mighty and Majestic, every day twelve rakas as voluntary prayer apart from the obligatory prayer, and he mentioned the like of it."
"27318","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Ali, meaning Ibn Mubarak, narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salama, from Abu Sufyan ibn Said al-Akhnas, he said: I entered upon Umm Habiba, and she called for sawiq for me and I drank it, and she said: Will you not perform ablution? I said: I have not broken my ablution. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"27319","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Sufyan ibn al-Mughira ibn al-Akhnas, that he entered upon Umm Habiba, and she gave him sawiq to drink, then he stood to pray, and she said to him: Perform ablution, O son of my brother, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Perform ablution from what fire has touched."
"27320","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shuayb narrated to us, he said: al-Zuhri said: Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman informed me that Abu Sufyan ibn Said ibn al-Akhnas informed him, from Umm Habiba the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she is the maternal aunt of Abu Sufyan ibn Said, and he mentioned the hadith."
"27321","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: And Ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Abu Salama ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, from Abu Sufyan ibn Said ibn al-Akhnas ibn Shariq, he said: I entered upon Umm Habiba, and she was his maternal aunt, and she gave me a drink of sawiq, and when I stood she said to me: O my son, do not pray until you perform ablution, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to perform ablution from what fire has touched of food."
